@startuml sd-register-maintenance
skinparam style strictuml
autonumber
title SD - Register maintenance and update aircraft status

actor "Maintenance Technician" as User
participant "API Gateway" as GW
participant "MaintenanceController" as Ctrl
participant "MaintenanceService" as Svc
participant "AircraftClient" as AC
participant "Aircraft Service" as Aircraft
database "Maintenance DB" as DB
participant "MaintenanceReplicator" as Rep

User -> GW : POST /api/maintenance/records\nJWT + maintenance data
GW -> Ctrl : forwards request
Ctrl -> Svc : registerMaintenance(dto)
Svc -> AC : getAircraftModelName(registrationNumber)\n(if model omitted)
AC -> Aircraft : GET /internal/aircraft/instances/{reg}
Aircraft --> AC : model data
AC --> Svc : model name
Svc -> Svc : resolve template and create SCHEDULED record
Svc -> DB : save(record)
DB --> Svc : saved record
Svc -> AC : updateMaintenanceStatus(reg, UNDER_MAINTENANCE)
AC -> Aircraft : PATCH /internal/aircraft/instances/{reg}/maintenance-status\nX-API-Key
Aircraft --> AC : status update + grounding report
AC --> Svc : acknowledged
Svc -> Rep : replicateAcknowledged(record)
Rep -> Rep : queue newest record revision per peer
Rep --> Svc : acknowledged or queued for retry
Svc --> Ctrl : record view
Ctrl --> GW : 201 Created
GW --> User : 201 Created

note over Svc, Aircraft
If Aircraft Service is unavailable, the maintenance record remains
created and the status update is logged for later operational recovery.
end note

@enduml
